# Windows icons follow the latest build

Before finishing a task that built `slate.exe` or `native-file-atlas.exe`,
refresh Desktop, Start, and existing pins so those icons launch that build.

```powershell
.\scripts\install-shortcuts.ps1 -Configuration Debug    # after a debug build
.\scripts\install-shortcuts.ps1 -Configuration Release  # after a release build
```

Use the configuration just built. If both profiles were built, use the newer
executable. Skip this when the session did not build either app.

`scripts/build-release.ps1` and `scripts/run-both-dev.ps1` already do this.
The procedure lives in `docs/dev-loop.md` (Desktop shortcuts); do not invent
a second shortcut writer.
